IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `rra-retirement`

-- Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993, ss 2, 4, 6, 7, 7A, 7B, 7C, 11A -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_retirement-and-re-employment-act-1993_baseline.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- Prescribed ages in every fixture are HYPOTHETICAL (minimum retirement age 63, re-employment age 68): the Gazette
-- notifications that set them are not deposited.

§ `Fixtures`

`a 60-year-old with no retirement age in her contract` MEANS `My employment` WITH
    `my age` IS 60
    `my prescribed minimum retirement age` IS 63
    `the retirement age stipulated in my contract` IS NOTHING
    `my prescribed re-employment age` IS 68
    `my year of birth` IS 1966
    `my month of birth` IS 3
    `my employer assesses my work performance as at least satisfactory` IS TRUE
    `my employer has proved on a balance of probabilities that I am not medically fit` IS FALSE
    `I have told my employer I will not continue working for it from my specified age` IS FALSE
    `my employer cannot find me a suitable vacancy despite reasonable attempts` IS FALSE
    `I accepted another employer's offer to employ me in place of my employer` IS FALSE

